# Crush 80 ZMK Project

## Build & Flash
- Build: `bash build.sh --skip-bridge --skip-mcuboot`
- Flash: `bash flash.sh` (or `bash flash.sh --build` for build+flash)
- Recovery: `python3 scripts/recovery_flash.py` (unplug/replug race)

## Critical Safety Rules
1. NEVER set `CONFIG_LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL=4` — floods serial, bricks SMP
2. NEVER enable HSPI (`&hspi { status = "okay" }`) — PE0/PE1/PE2 are matrix columns
3. Always confirm after flash: `mcumgr image confirm ""`
4. If SMP times out after flash, use recovery_flash.py (unplug/replug)

## Architecture
- MCUboot at 0x0, ZMK app at 0x10000, slot 1 at 0x80000
- Flash via MCUboot swap: upload → test hash → reset → wait 12s → confirm
- Serial port: /dev/cu.usbmodem1101 at 115200 baud
- mcumgr CLI: ~/go/bin/mcumgr

## GPIO Pin Assignments (CONFIRMED from original firmware binary)
- Columns (0-15): PE0, PE1, PE2, PE4, PE5, PE6, PB0, PB1, PB2, PB3, PB4, PB5, PB6, PC0, PC1, PC4
- Rows (0-5): PD7, PD2, PD3, PD4, PD5, PD6
- Source: Ghidra analysis of FUN_ram_0001a140 calls at offset 0xF078-0xF188

## Keymap Config
- Source of truth: ~/.config/DOTFILES/keybindings/crush80-zmk/
- build.sh syncs from dotfiles into repo before building
- Edit keymap there, then just run `bash flash.sh --build`

## Debugging
- Test SMP: `~/go/bin/mcumgr --conntype serial --connstring "dev=/dev/cu.usbmodem1101,baud=115200" echo hello`
- Check image: `mcumgr image list`
- Reset: `mcumgr reset`
- For kscan debugging, use CONFIG_ZMK_LOG_LEVEL_DBG=y (NOT LOG_DEFAULT_LEVEL=4)
- Read serial logs: open port with DTR=True via pyserial
